Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Formal Symbols in \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979828235121097*^9, 3.979828243095413*^9}, {
  3.979981066201235*^9, 3.979981069318391*^9}, {3.979983198861205*^9, 
  3.979983208054658*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c869a8dc-faf4-4ea4-bb7c-\
f90fc65907d7"],

Cell["\<\
Brian Beckman
Feb 2026\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9798282476706247`*^9, 3.9798282824743547`*^9}, 
   3.9799810774536133`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e8db9481-3cd4-4ad5-80d5-\
3aa4609ccce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In many tensorial calculations in \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD], we \
see formal symbols like ",
 StyleBox["\[FormalZ]", "Input"],
 " or extended formal symbols like ",
 StyleBox["\[FormalM]123", "Input"],
 ". Formal symbols, extended or not, are like ordinary symbols, except they\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]re protected: you can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t assign values to \
them without purposefully unprotecting them. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97998322473521*^9, 3.9799832455021467`*^9}, {
  3.979984101387508*^9, 3.97998414531249*^9}, {3.979984175793035*^9, 
  3.9799842385790854`*^9}, {3.9799842745615997`*^9, 3.9799843562092752`*^9}, {
  3.979984391002839*^9, 3.979984446043758*^9}, {3.979988961202718*^9, 
  3.9799890237923193`*^9}, {3.979989057344571*^9, 3.979989084403966*^9}, {
  3.979989114605278*^9, 3.9799891427942247`*^9}, {3.9799891740305634`*^9, 
  3.979989185101144*^9}, {3.97998955003321*^9, 
  3.979989580909987*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"83cf4a57-83ec-474c-a39c-\
c70f4ab5c00b"],

Cell["\<\
Mathematica directly supports \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Pure System\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] formal symbols, consisting of exactly one formal \
character. All such formal characters are listed below. We need extended \
formal symbols, with some non-formal characters after an initial formal \
character, because we need generated symbols guaranteed not to collide with \
other symbols. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97998322473521*^9, 3.9799832455021467`*^9}, {
  3.979984101387508*^9, 3.97998414531249*^9}, {3.979984175793035*^9, 
  3.9799842385790854`*^9}, {3.9799842745615997`*^9, 3.9799843562092752`*^9}, {
  3.979984391002839*^9, 3.979984446043758*^9}, {3.979988961202718*^9, 
  3.9799890237923193`*^9}, {3.979989057344571*^9, 3.979989084403966*^9}, {
  3.979989114605278*^9, 3.9799891427942247`*^9}, {3.9799891740305634`*^9, 
  3.979989185101144*^9}, {3.97998955003321*^9, 
  3.979989614890375*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b5f127a6-33a8-476d-a222-\
6715721de3f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Wolfram does not offer ",
 StyleBox["FormalSymbolQ", "Input"],
 ", so we implement it here. Extended formal symbols are an invention: \
Wolfram knows nothing about them, so we implement a constructor, ",
 StyleBox["CreateExtendedFormal", "Input"],
 ", and a predicate, ",
 StyleBox["FormalSymbolExtendedQ", "Input"],
 ". A formal symbol is reckoned \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["Extended", "Input"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] if it has correct syntax and has the Protected \
attribute."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979984450960313*^9, 3.9799846165829773`*^9}, {
  3.979989699221966*^9, 3.979989765860838*^9}, {3.979989817380724*^9, 
  3.979989856640547*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"31026b68-88ea-4e9c-ad01-\
a87d800b73c3"],

Cell["\<\
A symbol can be a formal symbol, an extended formal symbol, or neither, but \
never both.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979984450960313*^9, 3.9799846165829773`*^9}, {
  3.979989701755196*^9, 
  3.9799897020834084`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0d966852-7b48-4102-b2a5-\
1beeffc30da9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We further implement a ",
 StyleBox["SymbolInspector", "Input"],
 " for human monitoring and debugging of formal symbols."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9799846430724497`*^9, 
  3.9799846869369*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d567183d-617d-4d64-96d0-896b62258a8f"],

Cell["\<\
This exercise blossomed into a self-taught master class in evaluation \
control. The last section of this notebook presents our learnings. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979984695383939*^9, 3.979984765712696*^9}, 
   3.9799892832474527`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"17554550-8b5a-48a8-b38a-\
1f0593ab065b"],

